  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local Works Road Traffic Injuries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAIDs Local Works support in Angola partners with local universities to address road traffic injuries and deaths, a major public health and economic challenge in the country. The activity strengthens locally led research, data use, and community-based approaches to identify road safety risks and advance practical prevention measures, particularly along key transport corridors. By building Angolan institutional capacity and supporting locally driven solutions, the activity aims to reduce preventable injuries and deaths, protect human capital, and promote safer mobility linked to Angolas broader development and economic growth.</narrative>
  </description>
